00:55:29,745 --> 00:55:32,786
[SPEAKER_14]: Thank you, Mr. Murphy, and thank you for having me this evening to talk about the budget.

487
00:55:33,906 --> 00:55:45,228
[SPEAKER_14]: Within the school counseling and behavioral health department, there are several different positions, and I'll just review them again so that there's more clarity on when I'm discussing the position titles, because they're very similar.

488
00:55:46,288 --> 00:55:56,690
[SPEAKER_14]: School adjustment counselors are also called school social workers, and those are counselors who are managing the day-to-day individual and group counseling for students.

489
00:55:57,062 --> 00:56:05,225
[SPEAKER_14]: They also work on FBAs, their community liaisons, and they provide consults to anyone in the school building and parents as well.

490
00:56:05,985 --> 00:56:15,569
[SPEAKER_14]: School counselors, who are also referred to as guidance counselors, perform classes and lessons, both at the middle school and at the high school.

491
00:56:16,529 --> 00:56:22,851
[SPEAKER_14]: They also provide individual group counseling, but they carry the bulk of the academic transition and post-secondary planning.

492
00:56:23,091 --> 00:56:24,012
[SPEAKER_14]: They also coordinate our 504s.

493
00:56:25,579 --> 00:56:28,041
[SPEAKER_14]: facilitate parent meetings and provide academic supports.

494
00:56:29,001 --> 00:56:36,666
[SPEAKER_14]: Our school psychologists perform the psychological evaluations for special education and also provide counseling individual and group.

495
00:56:38,426 --> 00:56:43,950
[SPEAKER_14]: We also have within our department for BCBAs board certified behavior analysts.

496
00:56:44,370 --> 00:56:51,915
[SPEAKER_14]: They conduct observations and write support plans, consult with faculty and staff, provide trainings and conduct functional behavior assessments.

497
00:56:52,596 --> 00:56:55,618
[SPEAKER_14]: Behavior specialists are also under this team.

498
00:56:56,098 --> 00:56:57,439
[SPEAKER_14]: We have five district wide.

499
00:56:57,479 --> 00:56:59,300
[SPEAKER_14]: They are all based on the elementary level.

500
00:56:59,881 --> 00:57:04,224
[SPEAKER_14]: Prior to this year, we had one who was working with specialized programming.

501
00:57:04,824 --> 00:57:05,585
[SPEAKER_14]: We have increased

502
00:57:06,667 --> 00:57:19,716
[SPEAKER_14]: to five this year to mitigate some of the challenges from coming back in from the pandemic that we expected, with students needing more supports with routines and classroom teachers meeting more assistance with behavior plans.

503
00:57:22,538 --> 00:57:26,381
[SPEAKER_14]: There's also, as I've discussed earlier this year,

504
00:57:28,698 --> 00:57:31,699
[SPEAKER_14]: obviously an increase in need for mental health for our students.

505
00:57:32,100 --> 00:57:34,101
[SPEAKER_14]: This is not like breaking news.

506
00:57:34,161 --> 00:57:45,246
[SPEAKER_14]: We've all seen it all over the place, certainly with adolescents, but also with our youngest learners, elementary students, children all over the place are experiencing more mental health challenges than ever before.

507
00:57:46,186 --> 00:57:48,247
[SPEAKER_14]: And certainly there is a need

508
00:57:48,747 --> 00:57:54,531
[SPEAKER_14]: to increase supports in our district to meet the level of care to provide to those students.

509
00:57:55,071 --> 00:58:05,959
[SPEAKER_14]: We have seen over the course of this year an uptick in crisis management to include students having mobile crisis evaluations or being hospitalized for psychiatric emergencies.

510
00:58:06,759 --> 00:58:13,864
[SPEAKER_14]: We've also seen students who just need more care coming into the building and support throughout the day.

511
00:58:15,266 --> 00:58:20,489
[SPEAKER_14]: Mr. Murphy, it's okay with you, I'll go through the positions specifically, or do you want me to wait for that?

512
00:58:21,710 --> 00:58:28,913
[SPEAKER_07]: I think do school adjustment councils now and then we'll talk a little bit about the career counselor position after that.

513
00:58:29,514 --> 00:58:30,034
[SPEAKER_04]: Excellent.

514
00:58:30,294 --> 00:58:32,095
