530
00:59:48,141 --> 00:59:49,642
[SPEAKER_04]: So thank you and appreciate it.

531
00:59:50,183 --> 00:59:50,483
[SPEAKER_14]: Thank you.

532
00:59:52,308 --> 01:00:12,845
[SPEAKER_14]: So through the analysis of looking at the services, both of what students were requiring and what the MASCA, which is the Massachusetts Association of School Counseling, is recommending for a ratio, I've determined that three additional school adjustment counselors is necessary for next year.

533
01:00:13,065 --> 01:00:15,928
[SPEAKER_14]: The first would be an additional school adjustment counselor at the Brooks.

534
01:00:16,748 --> 01:00:20,171
[SPEAKER_14]: The Brooks, as of a few weeks ago, their roster was 527 students.

535
01:00:22,243 --> 01:00:34,967
[SPEAKER_14]: If we're increasing by 1.0 school adjustment counselors, counting the school psychologist as a 0.5 counselor, because she does do a lot of counseling as well as evaluations, this would lead us to a ratio of 210 to one for counseling.

536
01:00:35,668 --> 01:00:40,329
[SPEAKER_14]: Considering their specialized programming needs, this seems like an appropriate ratio for that school building.

537
01:00:42,050 --> 01:00:47,071
[SPEAKER_14]: The other priority here was to reduce the split positions.

