01:07:59,748 --> 01:08:02,509
[SPEAKER_07]: and what it would position the department to do.

616
01:08:03,750 --> 01:08:04,470
[SPEAKER_14]: Thank you very much.

617
01:08:05,651 --> 01:08:15,375
[SPEAKER_14]: A role shift in this year, school year 21-22, transformed the previous school community counselor position to a house counselor at the high school.

618
01:08:15,879 --> 01:08:24,764
[SPEAKER_14]: And this was for a very significant reason in terms to have two school counselors per house and not to have that divided counseling split.

619
01:08:25,305 --> 01:08:35,231
[SPEAKER_14]: Also the efforts of the school community counselor were somewhat halted due to the pandemic and what students were able to experience or be involved in at the time.

620
01:08:37,032 --> 01:08:38,533
[SPEAKER_14]: I would like to restore that position.

621
01:08:38,553 --> 01:08:42,175
[SPEAKER_14]: And the reason why is that it includes the following responsibilities.

622
01:08:42,415 --> 01:08:44,897
[SPEAKER_14]: Now that students are out and about going back to

623
01:08:45,737 --> 01:09:03,231
[SPEAKER_14]: more activities through the pandemic, there is a need for someone to be coordinating some of these events, which include managing our community service programs for all students, tracking their 60-hour graduation requirements, maintaining developing relationships with surrounding organizations for student community service opportunities.

624
01:09:03,371 --> 01:09:08,975
[SPEAKER_14]: As you can imagine, a lot of our students need support in terms of finding those opportunities within our community.

625
01:09:10,016 --> 01:09:11,617
[SPEAKER_14]: Also coordinating college rep visits.

626
01:09:12,538 --> 01:09:15,200
[SPEAKER_14]: Those had obviously been stopped for a period of time,

627
01:09:15,724 --> 01:09:19,546
[SPEAKER_14]: and we need those to resume again with vigor next year.

628
01:09:19,987 --> 01:09:31,013
[SPEAKER_14]: Supporting students finding employment opportunities, assisting with a local job fair, and managing our dual enrollment programs, which we have partnerships with Ben Franklin and Bunker Hill.

629
01:09:31,514 --> 01:09:40,559
[SPEAKER_14]: We have been in discussions with Bunker Hill to increase our dual enrollment program, which would require an advisor to oversee these students.

630
01:09:40,659 --> 01:09:44,722
[SPEAKER_14]: We are looking to have this opportunity for at least 30 of our students.

631
01:09:45,122 --> 01:09:48,063
[SPEAKER_14]: to have increased dual enrollment opportunities with Bunker Hill.

632
01:09:49,764 --> 01:10:03,150
[SPEAKER_14]: There's also a need to connect more of our students with just the community at large and to assist in finding them with low or no cost ways to be involved in the community.

633
01:10:03,811 --> 01:10:08,233
