1031
01:50:28,007 --> 01:50:43,956
[SPEAKER_07]: And so we're looking at an estimated $20,000 or so investment in musical instruments to make sure that we never have a... First of all, so that we can attract even more students into some of the programs and that we can make sure that our music classes are

1032
01:50:44,612 --> 01:50:59,258
[SPEAKER_07]: are well positioned in terms of the equipment they need, but also to make sure that we have the level of accessibility that we need to meet students' needs, regardless of whatever other challenges they may be experiencing.

1033
01:51:00,018 --> 01:51:12,883
[SPEAKER_07]: On the note of just making sure that we're keeping students engaged, we had a successful music summer camp program that brought in a significant number of students last summer.

1034
01:51:14,691 --> 01:51:24,896
[SPEAKER_07]: that's been able to be scheduled in the latter part of August to make sure that it's not conflicting with some of the other summer programming that we have scheduled for the summer of 2022.

1035
01:51:25,896 --> 01:51:32,580
[SPEAKER_07]: And so we'll be investing in that again and going out and making sure that students and families are aware of that.

1036
01:51:32,600 --> 01:51:35,341
[SPEAKER_07]: So it's something that they could address.

1037
01:51:35,741 --> 01:51:39,163
[SPEAKER_07]: And then on the visual arts side of the organization,

1038
01:51:40,819 --> 01:51:48,184
[SPEAKER_07]: in order to begin sort of thinking about the culture and climate issues that school communities are facing coming out of this period of significant disruption.

1039
01:51:49,004 --> 01:52:04,393
[SPEAKER_07]: We're looking at investments, ESSER funded investments in some programming that's been requested by the art educators as well as setting up some community art displays that will help to enliven each of our school communities.

1040
01:52:04,433 --> 01:52:09,176
[SPEAKER_07]: And so those are modest investments, but we think reflective of the broader priorities and goals

1041
01:52:09,826 --> 01:52:13,247
[SPEAKER_07]: and we wanted to just make sure that we had the opportunity to bring them to your attention.

1042
01:52:13,967 --> 01:52:22,368
[SPEAKER_07]: These last two rows speak to our stated goal of trying to reduce the fee-based services.

1043
01:52:22,388 --> 01:52:35,110
