1051
01:53:28,750 --> 01:53:30,772
[SPEAKER_04]: around differentiation of curriculum.

1052
01:53:30,812 --> 01:53:40,639
[SPEAKER_04]: So for the inclusion, we see a higher number of occlusion opportunities in these specials, specifically music arts, PE.

1053
01:53:41,640 --> 01:53:53,950
[SPEAKER_04]: And I know that we have, obviously we've had adaptive PE this year, which is really wonderful, but families have talked a lot about the lack of sort of differentiation in some music and art instruction, music,

1054
01:53:54,533 --> 01:53:57,854
[SPEAKER_04]: I think explicitly I've heard some and certainly the art.

1055
01:53:58,334 --> 01:54:08,236
[SPEAKER_04]: But so it, you know, as one can imagine, say in middle school, the students are learning about notes and sort of other aspects of theory and music instructions and what have you.

1056
01:54:08,817 --> 01:54:20,620
[SPEAKER_04]: A student perhaps with an intellectual disability or other disability, not being able to access that curriculum because there's not necessarily differentiation around what is being provided in the curriculum.

1057
01:54:21,440 --> 01:54:22,220
[SPEAKER_04]: Will any of this,

1058
01:54:23,555 --> 01:54:27,956
[SPEAKER_04]: sort of programmatic elements address that need.

1059
01:54:27,996 --> 01:54:29,577
[SPEAKER_04]: And again, I don't know if this is for Ms.

1060
01:54:29,617 --> 01:54:39,000
[SPEAKER_04]: Bowen or sort of just a question that I'm putting out in the air that we can address later, but it is something that I wanted to bring to folks' attention as something that's been brought to mind.

1061
01:54:39,440 --> 01:54:39,800
[SPEAKER_04]: Thank you.

1062
01:54:40,820 --> 01:54:41,840
[SPEAKER_07]: I'll certainly defer to Ms.

1063
01:54:41,860 --> 01:54:50,783
[SPEAKER_07]: Bowen if she wants to expand upon this, but I will say on the musical instrument side, challenges very similar to what you're describing.

1064
01:54:51,728 --> 01:54:58,714
[SPEAKER_07]: were explicitly stated as one of the reasons that this was something that we needed to address.

1065
01:54:58,914 --> 01:55:18,770
[SPEAKER_07]: And while I can assure you that this is not the case for every single one of the priorities that have been discussed tonight, the number that was requested was lower than the number that we ultimately projected based on the level of concern that was met by the sort

