[SPEAKER_07]: sort of anecdotal information that was presented.

1067
01:55:22,025 --> 01:55:36,637
[SPEAKER_07]: The idea that we could have a student that we, you know, I don't think this is true widespread, so I don't want to suggest that somehow this is indicative of an issue that's overwhelmingly pervasive.

1068
01:55:38,358 --> 01:55:46,865
[SPEAKER_07]: But the idea that we could have a student unable to, you know, play the instrument that he or she wants because,

1069
01:55:48,294 --> 01:55:51,796
[SPEAKER_07]: we don't have enough of them to modify it, is totally unacceptable.

1070
01:55:52,416 --> 01:56:02,163
[SPEAKER_07]: And so I appreciate the educators in the music area who raised this concern, Dr. Ricciardelli, for voicing it.

1071
01:56:02,664 --> 01:56:11,330
[SPEAKER_07]: And ultimately, based on that conversation, it's a slightly greater investment than was originally requested because I think to your point, Ms.

1072
01:56:11,350 --> 01:56:16,654
