1371
02:29:18,478 --> 02:29:20,859
[SPEAKER_07]: That's my opinion.

1372
02:29:20,919 --> 02:29:21,860
[SPEAKER_06]: Thank you, Mr. Sawyer.

1373
02:29:22,080 --> 02:29:34,387
[SPEAKER_07]: I'd be more than happy to present that information, but I think the one clarifying point that I want to make is that this is a most of these are all priorities that we think are absolutely worthy of public discussion.

1374
02:29:34,897 --> 02:29:36,958
[SPEAKER_07]: and making sure that the committee is aware of.

1375
02:29:37,518 --> 02:29:42,201
[SPEAKER_07]: They will not necessarily all make it into the superintendent's recommendation to you.

1376
02:29:43,102 --> 02:29:46,243
[SPEAKER_07]: There's still ongoing administrative vetting.

1377
02:29:46,724 --> 02:29:57,610
[SPEAKER_07]: And so while these priorities in a vacuum, frankly, if there wasn't some value to them, and in most cases, significant value, we wouldn't be taking up the committee or the community's time with them.

1378
02:29:59,119 --> 02:30:04,824
[SPEAKER_07]: our responsibility to sort of look at the budget as one complete coherent piece of information.

1379
02:30:04,904 --> 02:30:09,548
[SPEAKER_07]: It may be the case that there are some things that don't necessarily make it into that recommendation.

1380
02:30:09,608 --> 02:30:14,411
[SPEAKER_07]: So happy to provide all of that data so that you can see it and see the price tags.

1381
02:30:14,732 --> 02:30:22,418
[SPEAKER_07]: And I frankly think that's helpful for the community to see that the school department is not just showing up and asking to fund every priority we can think of.

1382
02:30:23,519 --> 02:30:27,582
[SPEAKER_07]: And I believe, understand that this list does not represent every priority we could think of.

1383
02:30:27,622 --> 02:30:28,523
[SPEAKER_07]: We're very imaginative

1384
02:30:29,584 --> 02:30:33,086
[SPEAKER_07]: There could be an endless list of ways that we could help students.

1385
02:30:34,066 --> 02:30:46,372
[SPEAKER_07]: But I think there is a responsibility to present something that is coherent and also within a certain degree of financial boundaries so that we can have a constructive conversation with the municipal government going forward.

1386
02:30:47,832 --> 02:30:48,173
[SPEAKER_13]: Thank you.

1387
02:30:48,673 --> 02:30:52,414
[SPEAKER_13]: I just, you know, we have the new math curriculum.

1388
02:30:52,655 --> 02:30:56,456
[SPEAKER_13]: That's a D or an E for the math coaches.

1389
02:30:58,496 --> 02:31:09,118
[SPEAKER_13]: And speaking to responsibility, purchasing something for which we cannot implement with fidelity is not responsible.

1390
02:31:10,158 --> 02:31:16,579
[SPEAKER_13]: And that's why the math coaches are so recommended and important for the curriculum.

1391
02:31:17,700 --> 02:31:25,061
[SPEAKER_13]: So I would just say that I want the community to know when we land on a number,

1392
02:31:25,750 --> 02:31:46,469
[SPEAKER_13]: because we will eventually land on a number, that here's the list of things, and if you cared about a full-time nurse at the Curtis Tufts, and that's C, D, or E, which forgive me for not having it memorized, that there was a way for us to have funded those, and it was not about what the school committee asked for.

1393
02:31:46,749 --> 02:31:47,830
[SPEAKER_13]: So I think that's a,

1394
02:31:50,908 --> 02:31:58,795
[SPEAKER_13]: You know, it's the awkwardness that the mayor is also the school committee chair that we have to talk about the mayor and the third person sometimes, which I think is very weird.

1395
02:31:58,875 --> 02:32:05,040
[SPEAKER_13]: But, you know, we do not have direct taxation and we can't run a deficit.

1396
02:32:05,140 --> 02:32:14,648
[SPEAKER_13]: So everything that people want that's not on that list already, that's where it isn't happening from is the,

1397
02:32:15,490 --> 02:32:17,312
[SPEAKER_13]: City is not allocating the resources.

1398
02:32:17,392 --> 02:32:24,300
[SPEAKER_13]: And Mr. Murphy does beat it up a little bit over and over again about how we're just part of the city's portfolio.

1399
02:32:24,480 --> 02:32:27,824
[SPEAKER_13]: But as is the case in many school committees, we are not.

1400
02:32:28,605 --> 02:32:34,912
[SPEAKER_13]: We have one responsibility, and it is not about how bad the roads are, how much money the rec department needs.

1401
02:32:35,478 --> 02:32:36,919
[SPEAKER_13]: have any other departments need money.

1402
02:32:36,959 --> 02:32:39,079
[SPEAKER_13]: That is not our responsibility to consider.

1403
02:32:39,239 --> 02:32:41,740
[SPEAKER_13]: We don't have any way to get information about their needs.

1404
02:32:42,201 --> 02:32:43,281
[SPEAKER_13]: How could we consider it?

1405
02:32:44,501 --> 02:32:55,586
[SPEAKER_13]: So I think that focusing on what the schools need to the complete exclusion of the other stuff, since we cannot ask or know anything about it is just responsible.

1406
02:32:55,626 --> 02:32:57,766
[SPEAKER_13]: I think it's the only reasonable thing.

1407
02:32:57,786 --> 02:33:00,527
[SPEAKER_13]: I mean, I think our roads are abysmal.

1408
02:33:00,667 --> 02:33:01,288
[SPEAKER_13]: I drive them too.

1409
02:33:03,240 --> 02:33:06,403
[SPEAKER_13]: but we and the school committee don't have anything to do with the roads.

1410
02:33:06,683 --> 02:33:09,105
[SPEAKER_13]: So thank you for your presentation tonight.

1411
02:33:09,125 --> 02:33:09,925
[SPEAKER_13]: I did appreciate it.

1412
02:33:13,528 --> 02:33:14,049
[SPEAKER_06]: Member Hayes.

1413
